Definition

An act of pretending to be someone else and convincing the data controller that the ill-intentioned individual is the data subject.

Brief History

Early Digital Era

In the 1960s, computer scientist Fernando Corbat at MIT introduced the concept of usernames and passwords to keep individual files private and secure on shared mainframes.";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:5:{s:31:"sidebar:glossary:phishing_scams";b:1;s:24:"sidebar:glossary:vishing";b:0;s:41:"sidebar:glossary:synthetic_identify_fraud";b:0;s:25:"sidebar:categories:ethics";b:1;s:29:"sidebar:categories:compliance";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Aditya Seth";}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1743108932;s:8:"modified";i:1743109251;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1743109251;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:39:"sidebar:categories:ethics:impersonation";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:1736;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Aditya Seth";}}}